{% extends '@CitadelAureum/core/docs/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block article %}
    <p>
        Aureum is your hotel's day-to-day operations desk. Everything staff need
        (bookings, deliveries, lost property, fines, the rooms directory, dining
        recommendations, and the events calendar) lives behind the menu on the left.
    </p>

    <h2>Finding your way around</h2>
    <p>
        The menu is split into groups. <strong>General</strong> holds the working
        modules you'll use every shift. <strong>Directory</strong> holds reference
        information: restaurants, rooms, and events. <strong>Manager</strong> only
        appears if your role includes management permissions.
    </p>
    <p>
        You only see the modules your role gives you access to. If something you
        need is missing from your menu, ask a manager to update your role.
        There's nothing to configure on your end.
    </p>

    <h2>Your dashboard</h2>
    <p>
        The dashboard is your start-of-shift briefing: items that need attention,
        activity this week, announcements from management, and upcoming events.
        Click any count to jump straight into the module behind it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
        Your account was created for you by a manager. On your very first login
        Aureum asks you to choose your own password before you can continue.
        You can change your password and timezone later under
        <strong>Settings</strong>.
    </p>

    <div class="au-docs-note">
        <i class="ph ph-info"></i>
        <p>
            Locked out or need access to another module? Your hotel's managers
            handle accounts and permissions; there is no self-service signup.
        </p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
